WEBVTT

00:00:48.560 --> 00:00:52.220
Ishtar... a goddess of ancient Babylonia.

00:00:53.100 --> 00:00:57.690
Ishtar rules over love and fertility, and also war.

00:00:59.070 --> 00:01:02.710
So she's the same as Aphrodite or Venus.

00:01:02.710 --> 00:01:06.040
No, she's the same as all women.

00:01:06.410 --> 00:01:07.470
Now that's...

00:01:08.550 --> 00:01:10.580
Kidokoro, so you know all about this?

00:01:10.580 --> 00:01:12.550
You've been studying.

00:01:12.550 --> 00:01:14.820
I'm just repeating what Dr. Madoka said.

00:01:28.070 --> 00:01:34.370
I haven't had time to worry about what kind of place this was, or what history it had.

00:01:34.740 --> 00:01:37.140
You've been too busy up till now.

00:01:41.980 --> 00:01:45.010
Yes... Yes, that's right.

00:01:47.450 --> 00:01:49.650
Yes, I see.

00:01:51.590 --> 00:01:54.390
Let's go back. They said a conclusion has been reached.

00:02:41.570 --> 00:02:43.880
What was the situation at the executives' meeting?

00:02:43.880 --> 00:02:46.140
You might say it was as expected.

00:02:46.140 --> 00:02:49.440
They all know we can't maintain the status quo.

00:02:50.350 --> 00:02:53.650
But there's the amount invested to consider.

00:02:59.420 --> 00:03:02.450
A conclusion has been reached about the pending concern.

00:03:03.600 --> 00:03:05.560
I will now present it to you.

00:03:07.800 --> 00:03:11.430
All Heaven's Gate projects will be discontinued.

00:03:14.740 --> 00:03:19.510
Delphys will be totally sealed off, all experimental subjects destroyed,

00:03:19.510 --> 00:03:22.170
...and this facility closed down within the year.

00:03:23.480 --> 00:03:28.440
This has been an extremely painful decision for us too.

00:03:29.090 --> 00:03:32.160
However, now that we understand that this mission invites...

00:03:32.160 --> 00:03:35.260
...a disaster unparalleled in human history, we must admit that...

00:03:35.260 --> 00:03:41.290
...to continue would be a breach of our ethics as scientists.

00:03:41.800 --> 00:03:46.860
Then you're saying what was written in Dr. Madoka's report was all correct?

00:03:48.340 --> 00:03:50.870
We feel justified in concluding so.

00:04:40.260 --> 00:04:42.660
I thought I'd play this for Delphys.

00:04:43.860 --> 00:04:46.520
If it's to be the last, it should be this piece.

00:04:53.810 --> 00:04:58.070
It all turned out as you said. Everything.

00:04:58.810 --> 00:05:01.640
This is where Gilgamesh's tomb was.

00:05:04.980 --> 00:05:08.350
I think that stood as a symbol for all of this.

00:05:21.070 --> 00:05:24.830
Listening to this on analog? I didn't realize you were so snobbish.

00:05:27.010 --> 00:05:29.570
You can't hear the full range in digital.

00:05:30.180 --> 00:05:32.340
The speakers are vacuum-tube too.

00:05:38.350 --> 00:05:39.980
I hear you're engaged.

00:05:41.250 --> 00:05:42.180
Yes...

00:05:43.460 --> 00:05:44.680
Congratulations.

00:06:17.520 --> 00:06:19.180
There's a problem in the underground facility!

00:06:23.060 --> 00:06:24.760
The main plant?

00:06:24.760 --> 00:06:29.430
It's the remaining test subjects! Lot number T-e-Ar.

00:06:29.700 --> 00:06:30.640
Tear!

00:06:30.640 --> 00:06:32.070
That's preposterous!

00:06:32.070 --> 00:06:33.940
It couldn't be terrorism, could it?

00:06:33.940 --> 00:06:38.100
We've got an ID on the intruder. It's Dr. Terumichi Madoka.

00:06:38.740 --> 00:06:40.480
Can we communicate directly with him?

00:06:40.480 --> 00:06:44.110
Dr. Madoka! Turn back immediately! This is dangerous!

00:06:44.420 --> 00:06:47.150
Do you know what you're doing?

00:06:47.150 --> 00:06:49.090
He'll reach Delphys shortly!

00:06:49.750 --> 00:06:51.880
This will be a disaster!

00:06:52.290 --> 00:06:54.160
Stop him at all costs!

00:06:54.160 --> 00:06:56.320
He's going through the physical lockdowns one after another!

00:06:57.060 --> 00:06:59.220
Twenty more seconds to Delphys!

00:07:03.270 --> 00:07:04.740
Dr. Madoka...

00:07:12.710 --> 00:07:14.200
So this is the end...

00:07:19.850 --> 00:07:22.250
In the middle of this century,

00:07:22.690 --> 00:07:26.750
...a single terrorist attack transformed the world.

00:07:28.990 --> 00:07:33.230
Sounds like a cartoon from the last century, I know,

00:07:33.230 --> 00:07:35.600
...but this really happened.

00:07:53.480 --> 00:07:57.010
The author of this event was Enkidu.

00:08:02.830 --> 00:08:04.850
Due to the date of its occurrence,

00:08:05.900 --> 00:08:09.060
...this incident came to be called Twin X.

00:08:12.740 --> 00:08:16.710
After Twin X, all computers became unusable,

00:08:16.710 --> 00:08:19.240
...and the advanced information civilization collapsed.

00:08:19.240 --> 00:08:22.650
Through war and starvation, most of the world's population was lost.

00:08:23.480 --> 00:08:26.920
In any case, this was all before I was born.

00:08:31.020 --> 00:08:34.720
Ever since I can remember, the sky has been veiled in a mirror.

00:08:36.030 --> 00:08:38.360
The Sheltering Sky...

00:08:39.300 --> 00:08:40.670
I don't really understand it,

00:08:40.670 --> 00:08:43.190
...but they say the phenomenon comes from a magnetic abnormality.

00:08:44.770 --> 00:08:46.900
Adults say it's eerie.

00:08:47.540 --> 00:08:51.270
But for us, this is the sky we're used to seeing.

00:09:08.190 --> 00:09:09.960
<i>Hey! Open up!</i>

00:09:09.960 --> 00:09:12.060
<i>Open up, you bastards!</i>

00:09:12.060 --> 00:09:15.130
<i>We know you're there!</i>

00:09:15.130 --> 00:09:16.790
<i>You're not gettin' away from us again!</i>

00:09:17.800 --> 00:09:20.130
<i>You playin' with us, little brats?</i>

00:09:27.150 --> 00:09:29.200
Enough games, you punks!

00:09:29.750 --> 00:09:31.280
I said open up!

00:09:32.520 --> 00:09:34.320
Little shits...

00:09:34.320 --> 00:09:39.160
Kiyoko, Tatsuya, you're in there, right?

00:09:39.160 --> 00:09:42.730
You keep running away, trying to get out of paying the money you owe.

00:09:42.730 --> 00:09:47.720
We know you are minors, but don't you see this is inexcusable?

00:10:06.780 --> 00:10:11.620
If the debt cannot be repaid, the young lady will provide us her body,

00:10:11.620 --> 00:10:15.720
...and her little brother will become an organ donor.

00:11:16.250 --> 00:11:17.620
Let's go.

00:11:18.120 --> 00:11:19.180
Yeah...

00:11:26.630 --> 00:11:27.800
Tatsuya?

00:11:27.800 --> 00:11:28.820
Bathroom.

00:11:29.970 --> 00:11:31.590
We need to hurry!

00:11:42.150 --> 00:11:43.610
Kiyoko...

00:11:45.220 --> 00:11:46.680
What?

00:11:54.490 --> 00:11:55.750
What's wrong?

00:11:57.360 --> 00:11:59.300
There's blood in it.

00:12:46.280 --> 00:12:49.580
Recently, they collapse a lot when it rains.

00:12:50.110 --> 00:12:54.520
I hear they cut a lot of corners on buildings made during the bubble.

00:12:57.260 --> 00:12:58.220
G...

00:13:00.360 --> 00:13:01.790
E-flat...

00:13:02.330 --> 00:13:05.020
Just 'cuz you have perfect pitch...

00:13:09.430 --> 00:13:10.730
So what about that?

00:13:14.070 --> 00:13:15.610
C-sharp...

00:13:15.610 --> 00:13:16.640
C...

00:13:16.640 --> 00:13:18.010
D...

00:13:18.010 --> 00:13:19.500
C-sharp...

00:13:23.880 --> 00:13:25.010
A...

00:13:35.190 --> 00:13:36.290
A tuning fork?

00:13:36.290 --> 00:13:37.760
Yeah...

00:13:44.370 --> 00:13:46.170
I'm hungry.

00:13:47.670 --> 00:13:49.140
Kiyoko!

00:14:21.070 --> 00:14:22.540
Tatsuya, this way!

00:14:40.290 --> 00:14:41.760
What was that?

00:15:02.150 --> 00:15:03.940
Where'd they go?!

00:15:11.520 --> 00:15:12.990
Tatsuya...

00:15:55.070 --> 00:15:57.160
This is a spooky house.

00:16:02.510 --> 00:16:03.970
What?

00:16:24.500 --> 00:16:25.960
Who's there?

00:16:28.200 --> 00:16:31.190
We're sorry. We had no idea anyone lived here.

00:16:33.800 --> 00:16:37.140
We're just keeping out of the rain too.

00:16:37.980 --> 00:16:39.700
What are...

00:16:44.450 --> 00:16:46.610
They're specimens of giant salamanders.

00:16:48.550 --> 00:16:51.250
What was in this place?

00:16:51.790 --> 00:16:55.320
Probably some kind of bio-research facility, I guess.

00:16:55.930 --> 00:16:59.660
They say salamanders were used in medicines.

00:16:59.660 --> 00:17:01.560
What's more, these are clones.

00:17:02.370 --> 00:17:03.830
Clones?

00:17:04.300 --> 00:17:07.830
They could do things like that in the old days. Come on.

00:17:19.080 --> 00:17:20.710
Well, come in.

00:17:35.570 --> 00:17:37.030
Hey...

00:17:39.500 --> 00:17:42.210
You're soaked. You'll catch cold.

00:17:42.210 --> 00:17:43.670
Here...

00:17:54.150 --> 00:17:55.450
A tuning fork?

00:18:00.660 --> 00:18:03.220
These people are taking shelter from the rain too.

00:18:03.490 --> 00:18:06.760
Really? Glad I made extra.

00:18:24.950 --> 00:18:25.880
Here you are.

00:18:30.190 --> 00:18:31.810
Ahh, warms you up.

00:18:34.830 --> 00:18:37.760
It'll get cold. Take it while it's hot.

00:18:38.260 --> 00:18:39.730
Well then...

00:18:46.700 --> 00:18:48.370
Sure keeps pouring.

00:18:50.470 --> 00:18:52.770
Are you all brothers?

00:18:55.210 --> 00:18:56.300
Why?

00:18:56.580 --> 00:18:58.780
Because you really look alike.

00:18:58.780 --> 00:19:00.510
Yeah, we're something like that.

00:19:00.990 --> 00:19:02.450
And you two?

00:19:03.790 --> 00:19:05.120
You're lovers?

00:19:06.020 --> 00:19:07.420
We're brother and sister!

00:19:12.830 --> 00:19:14.630
Who're those guys?

00:19:21.870 --> 00:19:23.640
Are those guys coming after you?

00:19:29.210 --> 00:19:30.870
You two stay here.

00:20:00.980 --> 00:20:04.380
We got them to go away for today, so relax.

00:20:45.690 --> 00:20:47.850
It's Toru. Can you hear me?

00:20:49.190 --> 00:20:51.250
Yes, I can hear you.

00:20:52.200 --> 00:20:55.170
I can also see what all of you see.

00:21:00.170 --> 00:21:01.760
So it's as we thought.

00:21:05.010 --> 00:21:07.200
Yes, it seems certain.

00:21:17.220 --> 00:21:18.950
At long last, they've stirred.

00:21:24.860 --> 00:21:26.190
Gilgamesh...

00:23:24.880 --> 00:23:26.820
Those people, do you think...

00:23:26.820 --> 00:23:28.150
We appreciate your concern, but we...

00:23:28.150 --> 00:23:28.850
Let's get away.

00:23:28.850 --> 00:23:29.620
We...

00:23:29.620 --> 00:23:31.190
It's about Dad, huh?

00:23:31.190 --> 00:23:32.360
The Countess?

00:23:32.360 --> 00:23:33.360
Let's get away!

00:23:33.360 --> 00:23:34.650
It couldn't be...

00:23:34.860 --> 00:23:36.690
What are you trying to do to us?

00:23:36.690 --> 00:23:37.960
Mom said so.

00:23:37.960 --> 00:23:41.870
She said there's no doubt people will come for us because of Dad.

00:23:41.870 --> 00:23:43.230
That kind of thing isn't for us.

00:23:43.230 --> 00:23:44.970
Say, what's this all about?

00:23:44.970 --> 00:23:47.340
If you've something to say, please say it here.

00:23:47.340 --> 00:23:49.310
Could you let us out now? Excuse me, driver!

00:23:49.310 --> 00:23:50.740
Let's get away!

00:23:50.740 --> 00:23:53.540
What's going to happen to us?
